{"id":"4be2e7ecc183d906","group":"93","path":"93/93-ex-algebraizable-propositional.md","title":"Algebraizable Propositional","display":"Algebraizable Propositional","type":"example","metadata":{"type":"example","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-ex-algebraizable-propositional","aliases":["93-ex-algebraizable-propositional"],"display":"Algebraizable Propositional","authors":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi","book_title":"Algebraizable Logics","depends_on":["[[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]]","[[93-df-algebraizable]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"example"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-ex-algebraizable-propositional"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-ex-algebraizable-propositional</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Algebraizable Propositional"},{"key":"authors","html":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi"},{"key":"book_title","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a55351eb48f8bd69\" href=\"?note=a55351eb48f8bd69\" title=\"93-df-algebraizable\">93-df-algebraizable</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"ex-algebraizable-propositional---Algebraizable-Propositional\">ex-algebraizable-propositional - Algebraizable Propositional</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span> are the concrete calculus, logic, language, signature, and generated Boolean-equivalent variety of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}\\)</span> is the concrete-presentation predicate defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e3c8f5c9e577b791\" href=\"?note=e3c8f5c9e577b791\" title=\"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus\">93-df-classical-propositional-calculus</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}\\)</span> is the explicitly signature-indexed algebraizability relation of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"a55351eb48f8bd69\" href=\"?note=a55351eb48f8bd69\" title=\"93-df-algebraizable\">93-df-algebraizable</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\n\\land\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93};\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\n\\land\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93};\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The algebraic semantics of classical logic was the paradigm case that\nmotivated the general theory of algebraizable logics developed by\nBlok and Pigozzi. The assertion now names a concrete proof relation and a\nsame-signature generated variety, rather than relying on an ambient object called “CPL.”</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"ex-algebraizable-propositional---Algebraizable-Propositional","text":"ex-algebraizable-propositional - Algebraizable Propositional","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebraizable","status":"resolved","id":"a55351eb48f8bd69","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-algebraizable]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}$, $\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}$, $\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}$, $\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}$, and $\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}$ are the concrete calculus, logic, language, signature, and generated Boolean-equivalent variety of [[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-classical-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"e3c8f5c9e577b791","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}$ is the concrete-presentation predicate defined in [[93-df-classical-propositional-calculus]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebraizable","status":"resolved","id":"a55351eb48f8bd69","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}$ is the explicitly signature-indexed algebraizability relation of [[93-df-algebraizable]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\n\\land\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf{BA}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93};\\tau^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}).","display":true}],"bytes":1556,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["e3c8f5c9e577b791","a55351eb48f8bd69"]}